    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been executed and recorded — 8 PASS, 11 FAIL.\n\n**Summary of findings:**\n\nThe app's search/browse, model opening, template browsing, graph rendering (directed, weighted, pannable/zoomable), summary-metric recalculation, gap detection and gap alerting all work correctly. Scenario tab switching also behaves as specified.\n\nThe failures cluster around three root defects:\n\n1. **The graph never re-renders after a state change** (`useNodesState`/`useEdgesState` are seeded once with no sync). This breaks FT-5 (disabled state invisible, re-enable impossible), FT-7 (applied template's competencies never appear in the graph), CT-16 (critical-path highlighting stale and contradicting the summary) and IX-20 (node controls show pre-edit values; subsequent edits restart from the original state, silently wiping earlier edits).\n2. **Simulation adjustments are uninitialized** (`adjustments` starts as `{}`), causing IX-19 (initial Recruitment run does nothing despite a success toast) and FT-10/CS-12 (choosing a level adjustment leaves the weight delta undefined → competency weights become `NaN` and Coverage renders \"NaN%\").\n3. **No persistence or edge editing** — Save and Save-as-Template are toast-only stubs with no storage and no name/description dialog (FT-8, FT-11), and relationship weights have no editing affordance at all (FT-4)."
  }
}
